00:10:45.810 --> 00:10:50.430
But also give a shout out to the Pixel 7A.

00:10:50.430 --> 00:10:52.350
As you probably remember,
the price went up this year,

00:10:52.350 --> 00:10:54.630
all the way up to 500 bucks.

00:10:54.630 --> 00:10:56.100
But it did gain some stuff.

00:10:56.100 --> 00:10:57.570
It has a 90 hertz display now.

00:10:57.570 --> 00:10:59.700
It has better specs, and it still does

00:10:59.700 --> 00:11:02.100
all the stuff that you
expect from a Pixel.

00:11:02.100 --> 00:11:05.250
So, it deserves a shout
out for being a good phone

00:11:05.250 --> 00:11:06.083
at that price.

00:11:06.083 --> 00:11:07.230
So then, next up.

00:11:07.230 --> 00:11:09.120
Best Battery.

00:11:09.120 --> 00:11:11.910
Best Battery overall in a smartphone.

00:11:11.910 --> 00:11:14.070
This doesn't necessarily go to the one

00:11:14.070 --> 00:11:16.590
that just has the
highest battery capacity.

00:11:16.590 --> 00:11:20.670
I'm more giving Best Overall
Battery Experience award.

00:11:20.670 --> 00:11:23.010
Ideally, you also have some
decently fast-charging,

00:11:23.010 --> 00:11:23.940
or wireless charging.

00:11:23.940 --> 00:11:25.770
Or, it's just convenient
that it lasts for so long.

00:11:25.770 --> 00:11:28.170
It might not actually be the biggest sell.

00:11:28.170 --> 00:11:30.120
I don't know that anyone's
actually buying a phone

00:11:30.120 --> 00:11:33.000
just because it has the
absolute best battery life.

00:11:33.000 --> 00:11:34.563
But if you do live that life,

00:11:35.777 --> 00:11:37.890
that no worries away from a charger life,

00:11:37.890 --> 00:11:40.290
you'll probably care about
the winners of this category.

00:11:40.290 --> 00:11:43.200
So my winner, who's getting a trophy

00:11:43.200 --> 00:11:48.200
for best battery this year is
iPhone 15 Plus, specifically.

00:11:49.350 --> 00:11:52.680
This thing just goes and goes, and goes.

00:11:52.680 --> 00:11:55.230
The bigger battery, in general,
has a lot to do with it.

00:11:55.230 --> 00:11:58.263
The 60 hertz display, also
has a lot to do with it.

00:11:59.338 --> 00:12:00.570
But, if you want a risk-free no-brainer

00:12:00.570 --> 00:12:02.430
great battery life, that's definitely

00:12:02.430 --> 00:12:03.660
gonna get it done for you.

00:12:03.660 --> 00:12:07.950
I'm also gonna give a shout
out to the ROG phone 7.

00:12:07.950 --> 00:12:09.180
It doesn't have wireless charging,

00:12:09.180 --> 00:12:10.500
but it does have pretty fast charging.

00:12:10.500 --> 00:12:12.540
And it has the biggest battery capacity

00:12:12.540 --> 00:12:13.710
of any phone I've used this year.

00:12:13.710 --> 00:12:16.830
6,000 milliamp powers.

00:12:16.830 --> 00:12:18.540
And if you drop it down to 60 hertz,

00:12:18.540 --> 00:12:21.510
it will also just go, and go, and go.

00:12:21.510 --> 00:12:26.310
And also, another Asus phone,
which is the Zenfone 10.

00:12:26.310 --> 00:12:28.560
This one kind of feels like wizard-like.

00:12:28.560 --> 00:12:31.560
I don't know how, because
it's not the biggest battery.

00:12:31.560 --> 00:12:35.351
It is pretty aggressive at
killing background apps,

00:12:35.351 --> 00:12:37.832
and it's probably missing
some bands in the U.S.

00:12:37.832 --> 00:12:39.456
So, that might have
something to do with it.

00:12:39.456 --> 00:12:42.810
But this phone, this small
5.9 inch display phone,

00:12:42.810 --> 00:12:44.160
it's killer battery life.

00:12:44.160 --> 00:12:46.110
It can be a two day phone.

00:12:46.110 --> 00:12:49.069
And you can drop it down
to 60 hertz, as well.

00:12:49.069 --> 00:12:51.480
So, whatever Asus is doing
over there, keep it up.

00:12:51.480 --> 00:12:53.190
Because battery life is great.

00:12:53.190 --> 00:12:54.900
I recently talked about
this in my hot takes video

00:12:54.900 --> 00:12:57.060
about how phones are getting
more and more powerful.

00:12:57.060 --> 00:12:59.640
But generally the average
battery life hasn't

00:12:59.640 --> 00:13:01.290
really changed that much.

00:13:01.290 --> 00:13:03.450
It's just been all day is good.

00:13:03.450 --> 00:13:05.610
So it's good to see some
phone actually pushing

00:13:05.610 --> 00:13:08.220
that envelope, and they
deserve to get rewarded for it.

00:13:08.220 --> 00:13:10.593
So then, Best Design.

00:13:11.539 --> 00:13:15.150
This one is so tough every time.

00:13:15.150 --> 00:13:15.983
Best Design.

00:13:15.983 --> 00:13:18.120
Because first of all,
design is subjective.

00:13:18.120 --> 00:13:21.690
Like something I find pretty,
you might find ugly. Fine.

00:13:21.690 --> 00:13:25.800
But also just in general, it
feels like every phone has

00:13:25.800 --> 00:13:28.890
some flaw, some reason why,

00:13:28.890 --> 00:13:30.420
and I can't give it to that one.

00:13:30.420 --> 00:13:31.680
Like think about it,
if you're in my shoes,

00:13:31.680 --> 00:13:32.940
you gotta give a design award, right?

00:13:32.940 --> 00:13:35.310
First of all, a lot of
phones look pretty similar

00:13:35.310 --> 00:13:37.350
to the way they did the
previous year, right?

00:13:37.350 --> 00:13:38.183
So I can't give it to one

00:13:38.183 --> 00:13:40.200
that looks exactly the same as last year.

00:13:40.200 --> 00:13:41.850
But also, I can't give it to one that has

00:13:41.850 --> 00:13:45.600
some fatal flow, if it's missing
a camera it should of had,

00:13:45.600 --> 00:13:47.820
or if it's missing, it has a crazy bezel.

00:13:47.820 --> 00:13:50.320
I can't give it to the one
with the biggest notch,

00:13:51.180 --> 00:13:52.590
or dynamic island, can I?

00:13:52.590 --> 00:13:54.870
I can't give it to the one
that's made of plastic,

00:13:54.870 --> 00:13:57.030
or the one that has a
curved display on the edges.

00:13:57.030 --> 00:13:59.910
Like what is an actually flawless,

00:13:59.910 --> 00:14:02.310
maybe it's the most boring design.

00:14:02.310 --> 00:14:03.780
But, you don't wanna give the design award

00:14:03.780 --> 00:14:06.330
to the most boring design.

00:14:06.330 --> 00:14:07.163
This is a hard one.

00:14:07.163 --> 00:14:08.730
And then it hit me.

00:14:08.730 --> 00:14:12.870
There was a phone this year
that basically made headlines

00:14:12.870 --> 00:14:14.760
just for its design.

00:14:14.760 --> 00:14:17.850
In a good way, and I agreed with them.

00:14:17.850 --> 00:14:20.340
And it absolutely deserves a
trophy for design this year.

00:14:20.340 --> 00:14:23.910
It's the Honor Magic V2.

00:14:23.910 --> 00:14:24.750
This thing right here.

00:14:24.750 --> 00:14:27.150
This phone legitimately
shifted the way I think

00:14:27.150 --> 00:14:28.470
about phone hardware.

00:14:28.470 --> 00:14:31.333
It was like a gear shift in
the world of foldable phones.

00:14:31.333 --> 00:14:33.540
A think a lot of us didn't even realize

00:14:33.540 --> 00:14:35.910
that you could make a phone like this.

00:14:35.910 --> 00:14:39.600
That has, first of all, it's
under 10 millimeters thick,

00:14:39.600 --> 00:14:40.530
when it's closed.

00:14:40.530 --> 00:14:43.740
Which is the same thickness
as plenty of regular phones.

00:14:43.740 --> 00:14:45.840
It has a full-sized screen on the outside.

00:14:45.840 --> 00:14:49.200
It has a corner-to-corner
foldable display on the inside.

00:14:49.200 --> 00:14:52.920
It somehow also fits a 5,000
million power total battery.

00:14:52.920 --> 00:14:56.370
Which I think is the biggest
I've seen in any foldable.

00:14:56.370 --> 00:14:59.670
Toss in 60 plus watt charging,
a triple camera setup,

00:14:59.670 --> 00:15:01.830
a terabyte of internal storage.

00:15:01.830 --> 00:15:03.750
I think a lot of us didn't
realize this was possible.

00:15:03.750 --> 00:15:04.800
So even though the rest of the phone

00:15:04.800 --> 00:15:05.970
might be a little questionable,

00:15:05.970 --> 00:15:08.610
maybe some weird software
that I wouldn't wanna use,

00:15:08.610 --> 00:15:11.580
the one thing that nobody
could question is the design.

00:15:11.580 --> 00:15:14.220
Everyone I've shown it to
universally is impressed

00:15:14.220 --> 00:15:15.630
in some way by it.

00:15:15.630 --> 00:15:20.400
But that actually brings us
to our first new category ad

00:15:20.400 --> 00:15:22.470
in a long time in the Smartphone Awards,

00:15:22.470 --> 00:15:25.410
and that is Best Foldable Phone.

00:15:25.410 --> 00:15:28.140
So this is the first time
genuinely separating out,

00:15:28.140 --> 00:15:30.900
and considering all of the folding phones

00:15:30.900 --> 00:15:32.640
that came out during the year.

00:15:32.640 --> 00:15:34.230
And the reason it's getting
its own category this year

00:15:34.230 --> 00:15:36.570
is because there's
genuinely a large variety

00:15:36.570 --> 00:15:40.980
of shapes and sizes and
versions of foldable phones,

00:15:40.980 --> 00:15:42.990
and flippable phones
that we can choose from.

00:15:42.990 --> 00:15:43.920
So I think in general,

00:15:43.920 --> 00:15:45.570
I made a video talking about this already.

00:15:45.570 --> 00:15:48.690
But folding phones are
quite on the doorstep yet.

00:15:48.690 --> 00:15:49.590
Like, they're close,

00:15:49.590 --> 00:15:53.370
but they're still mostly
thicker and more expensive

00:15:53.370 --> 00:15:54.780
than normal phones.

00:15:54.780 --> 00:15:56.310
But, I do wanna reward the ones

00:15:56.310 --> 00:15:59.010
that are pushing the
boundaries in some way

00:15:59.010 --> 00:16:00.720
towards that revolution.

00:16:00.720 --> 00:16:05.223
So, winner for best
foldable phone in 2023,

00:16:06.720 --> 00:16:09.480
yeah, that's the OnePlus Open.

00:16:09.480 --> 00:16:12.150
Man, this phone is good.

00:16:12.150 --> 00:16:14.430
When I was thinking about
what I would personally

00:16:14.430 --> 00:16:16.470
daily drive from the folding phones bunch,

00:16:16.470 --> 00:16:18.360
this is the one that bubbled to the top.

00:16:18.360 --> 00:16:20.910
This is folding phone I
would be most likely to use.

00:16:20.910 --> 00:16:24.480
When it's closed, it feels
the most like a normal phone.

00:16:24.480 --> 00:16:27.300
Mostly because the aspect
ratio on the size of the screen

00:16:27.300 --> 00:16:30.300
is normal phone-ish, flat sides.

00:16:30.300 --> 00:16:31.680
But then you open it up,

00:16:31.680 --> 00:16:34.530
and it's a nearly eight
inch, almost perfectly square

00:16:34.530 --> 00:16:37.080
folding screen with a very minimal crease.

00:16:37.080 --> 00:16:40.110
Awesome specs, really good software,

00:16:40.110 --> 00:16:41.580
and a lot of fun features to back it up.

00:16:41.580 --> 00:16:42.690
I think my favorite part is just the way

00:16:42.690 --> 00:16:44.280
you can move around multiple windows

00:16:44.280 --> 00:16:45.840
and keep them full-size.

00:16:45.840 --> 00:16:48.090
And have them overlap sort
of the edge of the screen.

00:16:48.090 --> 00:16:51.180
It's a fun and unique,
like actually new way

00:16:51.180 --> 00:16:52.950
of multi-tasking on a phone.

00:16:52.950 --> 00:16:53.880
And it actually works.

00:16:53.880 --> 00:16:56.070
This was the best phone
with a folding screen

00:16:56.070 --> 00:16:58.140
that was released during 2023.

00:16:58.140 --> 00:16:59.100
No doubt about that.

00:16:59.100 --> 00:17:01.680
It's also basically
the exact same hardware

00:17:01.680 --> 00:17:04.893
as the Oppo Find End Three Fold.

00:17:05.872 --> 00:17:07.890
So, shout out to that one, as well.

00:17:07.890 --> 00:17:09.510
But I also wanna give an
honorable mention here.

00:17:09.510 --> 00:17:10.950
I'm gonna actually say it's the runner-up

00:17:10.950 --> 00:17:12.753
in this category of best foldable.

00:17:14.577 --> 00:17:16.140
To the Pixel Fold.

00:17:16.140 --> 00:17:18.840
And that's just because
this one specifically

00:17:18.840 --> 00:17:22.560
is my favorite foldable to use closed.

00:17:22.560 --> 00:17:24.210
Because the outside screen is so good.

00:17:24.210 --> 00:17:26.310
The outside screen is nice and compact.

00:17:26.310 --> 00:17:29.580
It's the most reachable,
it's the smallest, also.

00:17:29.580 --> 00:17:33.090
But it's wide, it's big, it's
super useful to use closed.

00:17:33.090 --> 00:17:35.430
And for whatever reason,
I love that about it.

00:17:35.430 --> 00:17:37.620
I don't know if that's a
good thing or a bad thing,

00:17:37.620 --> 00:17:40.230
that I opened it way less.

00:17:40.230 --> 00:17:41.730
But it's the best to use closed.

00:17:41.730 --> 00:17:44.352
And, I'm gonna give an
honorable mention as well

00:17:44.352 --> 00:17:46.830
to Samsung's Z Flip 5.

00:17:46.830 --> 00:17:48.120
I mentioned it earlier in this video.

00:17:48.120 --> 00:17:49.830
But, a couple of things about this.

00:17:49.830 --> 00:17:51.810
One is, it feels like
it's leading the pack

00:17:51.810 --> 00:17:52.830
for the flipping phones.

00:17:52.830 --> 00:17:54.000
I think it's better than the Razer,

00:17:54.000 --> 00:17:56.670
I think it's better than some
of the other flipping ones.

00:17:56.670 --> 00:18:01.230
But also as far as build quality,
and just quality control,

00:18:01.230 --> 00:18:04.260
Samsung in general, is
at the top of the heap.

00:18:04.260 --> 00:18:06.030
Basically every other folding phone

00:18:06.030 --> 00:18:08.880
has had some level of
quality control issues

00:18:08.880 --> 00:18:10.920
at some point and some rate.

00:18:10.920 --> 00:18:12.510
And Samsung ironically, the ones that had

00:18:12.510 --> 00:18:14.070
the biggest issues at the beginning,

00:18:14.070 --> 00:18:16.380
have ironed it out the most over time.

00:18:16.380 --> 00:18:18.600
So that's their reward
for jumping in early.

00:18:18.600 --> 00:18:20.750
Also, I have to give
that honorable mention

00:18:21.709 --> 00:18:24.857
to the Honor Magic E2,
just purely for the design.

00:18:24.857 --> 00:18:26.250
I still can't believe
they made this phone.

00:18:26.250 --> 00:18:27.083
Super-impressive.

00:18:27.083 --> 00:18:30.330
So, next award, Most Improved.

00:18:30.330 --> 00:18:31.983
The Most Improved Award.

00:18:33.120 --> 00:18:34.770
Hmm.

00:18:34.770 --> 00:18:36.600
It's interesting because again,

00:18:36.600 --> 00:18:38.640
lots of phones play it safe.

00:18:38.640 --> 00:18:42.270
Lots of phones are just a
slight evolution from last year.

00:18:42.270 --> 00:18:43.860
They're a slight spec bump.

00:18:43.860 --> 00:18:46.230
And I can't get mad at that if
they're already a good phone.

00:18:46.230 --> 00:18:48.150
Like Zenfone, for example.

00:18:48.150 --> 00:18:50.580
I'm happy they kept a
lot of things the same.

00:18:50.580 --> 00:18:52.470
But then, that makes
the Most Improved Award

00:18:52.470 --> 00:18:56.430
a little more of a quirky pick.

00:18:56.430 --> 00:18:58.710
Maybe not the most
obvious pick in the world.

00:18:58.710 --> 00:19:02.910
But I'm gonna go with the Nothing Phone 2.

00:19:02.910 --> 00:19:04.950
Most Improved Phone 2023.

00:19:04.950 --> 00:19:07.020
So this is part hardware story,

00:19:07.020 --> 00:19:08.490
and part a software story.

00:19:08.490 --> 00:19:10.110
So obviously, they didn't
change the hardware

00:19:10.110 --> 00:19:12.270
a ton from the first Nothing Phone.

00:19:12.270 --> 00:19:13.620
Because they're literally brand new,

00:19:13.620 --> 00:19:15.300
so they're just getting
their identity set.

00:19:15.300 --> 00:19:18.090
So yeah, there's a newer,
higher resolution LED pattern

00:19:18.090 --> 00:19:18.930
on the back.

00:19:18.930 --> 00:19:20.580
There is a slightly curved glass now

00:19:20.580 --> 00:19:21.810
to feel a little better in the hand.

00:19:21.810 --> 00:19:23.970
But generally, it still
looks like a nothing phone.

00:19:23.970 --> 00:19:26.430
But they also did a lot with the software,

00:19:26.430 --> 00:19:31.200
specifically moving to
Nothing OS 2.0 and then 2.5.

00:19:31.200 --> 00:19:33.270
Which now on Android 14.

00:19:33.270 --> 00:19:35.160
Which gets a lot of new
stuff with this phone.

00:19:35.160 --> 00:19:37.500
There's a focus on
efficiency and smoothness,

00:19:37.500 --> 00:19:38.850
and then adding all these features.

00:19:38.850 --> 00:19:40.470
And there's also been fantastic.

00:19:40.470 --> 00:19:42.840
So you combine that with the new specs,

00:19:42.840 --> 00:19:44.640
the slightly bumped design,

00:19:44.640 --> 00:19:46.950
and then a bunch of the new
features that unfortunately

00:19:46.950 --> 00:19:48.840
the Phone 1.0 isn't getting,

00:19:48.840 --> 00:19:51.870
like the better glif controls,
and clone app feature,

00:19:51.870 --> 00:19:53.640
and monochrome theme and stuff.

00:19:53.640 --> 00:19:56.100
It just adds up to a
pretty big improvement.

00:19:56.100 --> 00:19:57.360
To the point where in this world

00:19:57.360 --> 00:20:00.060
with most people just being
able to buy last year's phone

00:20:00.060 --> 00:20:01.020
and be totally fine.

00:20:01.020 --> 00:20:02.400
With this phone, I would actually say,

00:20:02.400 --> 00:20:03.930
don't buy last year's phone.

00:20:03.930 --> 00:20:06.510
You should just get the
Phone 2, over the Phone 1.

00:20:06.510 --> 00:20:08.550
Plus you can send blue bubbles to,

00:20:08.550 --> 00:20:11.070
oh, wait, sorry never
mind, you can't do that.

00:20:11.070 --> 00:20:14.310
But still, Phone 2, much improved.

00:20:14.310 --> 00:20:16.320
It's probably gonna steady out after this.

00:20:16.320 --> 00:20:18.030
And this was nice to put them on the map.

00:20:18.030 --> 00:20:19.500
But now, they'll have to stabilize

00:20:19.500 --> 00:20:21.270
and become a real company.

00:20:21.270 --> 00:20:24.030
And you know what? Honorable Mention.

00:20:24.030 --> 00:20:26.460
Just because I don't know
if anyone else can say

00:20:26.460 --> 00:20:29.130
they technically made this
big of a change in their phone

00:20:29.130 --> 00:20:33.480
as much as switching the
iPhone 15 to USB type C.

00:20:33.480 --> 00:20:35.610
So, Honorable Mention to the iPhone.

00:20:35.610 --> 00:20:37.230
All right, next up.

00:20:37.230 --> 00:20:38.850
Bust of the Year.

00:20:38.850 --> 00:20:42.150
The award you don't
really wanna have to give,

00:20:42.150 --> 00:20:44.520
but one of these phones on this desk

00:20:44.520 --> 00:20:47.970
is gonna win Worse New Phone of 2023.

00:20:47.970 --> 00:20:50.220
Look, I do have to preface
this basically every time

00:20:50.220 --> 00:20:52.350
by saying, it is actually
genuinely hard now

00:20:52.350 --> 00:20:54.090
to get a bad phone.

00:20:54.090 --> 00:20:56.610
Like most phones, no matter
what price point you're at

00:20:56.610 --> 00:20:58.860
are either gonna be
really good for the money,

00:20:58.860 --> 00:21:00.150
or okay for the money.

00:21:00.150 --> 00:21:02.403
It's hard to get a bad phone.

00:21:03.420 --> 00:21:07.200
But there was one bad phone this year.

00:21:07.200 --> 00:21:09.150
And so, it's gonna win a trophy for it.

00:21:09.150 --> 00:21:14.150
And that would be Solama Saga Cryto Phone.

00:21:15.690 --> 00:21:16.530
Bust of the year.

00:21:16.530 --> 00:21:19.110
There is actually no price
that I would recommend

00:21:19.110 --> 00:21:20.490
anyone buys this phone.

00:21:20.490 --> 00:21:23.130
Buying this phone is
like buying a timeshare.

00:21:23.130 --> 00:21:26.580
It might seem like a good
idea for two seconds.

00:21:26.580 --> 00:21:28.140
But the second you actually do it,

00:21:28.140 --> 00:21:30.210
you realize how horrible
of an idea it was.

00:21:30.210 --> 00:21:32.490
And, this is just a bad phone.

00:21:32.490 --> 00:21:34.500
The one redeeming quality is actually

00:21:34.500 --> 00:21:36.810
it does have this nice build quality.

00:21:36.810 --> 00:21:39.633
It's got ceramic, and it's
nice and weighty and heavy.

